ask                                  see him as early as possible and advise          Maintains polite tone through the\n Write a referral letter to cardiologist Dr.   him on further management.\n Ken Wilson. Suite 5, Greenslopes                                                               use of modal verbs would & could\n Hospital Medical Centre, Brisbane 4121.       Yours sincerely                                  Uses appropriate expression: in\n                                                                                                order to rule out\n                                               Dr Z", "extraction": "text"}, {"number": 668, "text": "Assessment                                  I believe that Catherine needs an urgent\nDepression. Severe. ?Bi polar               psychiatric consultation regarding her           Summarises chief complaint in\nNeeds urgent treatment                      acute episode of depression and I would          original language\nCalled to husband                           appreciate it if you could take over her         Maintains polite tone through the\nWriting Task                                care for appropriate treatment.\nWrite a referral letter to psychiatrist                                                      use of modal verbs would & could\nDr. Abe Normal Brampston St, Mt                                                              Uses polite request for on going\nGravatt ,4121,QLD.                          Yours sincerely,                                 care\n\n                                            Dr X (GP)\n\nAssessment                                  I would appreciate your assessment and\nDiagnosed peritonitis with perforation      emergency management of this patient’s           Note, sometimes a brief\nWriting Task                                condition. If you need further information,      conclusion is all that is required....\nRefer urgently to the Emergency             please feel free to contact me.                  or all that you will have time for!\nDepartment Admitting Doctor\n                                            Yours sincerely,                                 Although it is a memorised phrase\n                                                                                             to some degree, it is\n                                            Dr X                                             grammatically correct, concise,\n                                                                                             direct and contains a level of\n                                                                                             urgency\n                                                                                             Maintains polite tone through the\n                                                                                             use of modal verb would\n                                                                                             Contains an offer of future\n                                                                                             support\n\n\n\n\n                                                        Common Errors\n                            Incorrect                                                         Correct\n\n    I would very much appreciated your attention regarding             I would very much appreciate your attention regarding\n    further management of Mr. Henderson.                               further management of Mr. Henderson.(active)\n                                                                       Your attention regarding further management of Mr.\nExplanation: Incorrect grammar, see above\n                                                                       Henderson would be very much appreciated.(passive)\n\n\n\n    If you have any query, please do not hesitate to contact           If you have any queries, please do 